1
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,530
You've seen better days, my lord.

2
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:12,620
Another visit?

3
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:17,090
It seems you're my last friend.

4
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:20,270
No no, many still love you.

5
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:25,080
Sansa came to court this morning to plead for your life.

6
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,540
On her knees, begging for me, hmmm.

7
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,540
Did you laugh with the others?

8
00:02:31,690 --> 00:02:33,090
You do me wrong, my lord.

9
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:35,330
Your blood is the last thing I want.

10
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:37,130
I don't know what you want.

11
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,640
I've given up trying to guess.

12
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,710
When I was still a boy...

13
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:48,290
before they cut my balls off with a hot knife...

14
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:52,290
I traveled with a group of actors through the free cities.

15
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:57,440
They taught me that each man has a role to play.

16
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:59,710
The same is true at court.

17
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:02,010
I am the Master of Whisperers.

18
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:06,480
My role is to be sly, obsequious and without scruples.

19
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,940
I'm a good actor, my lord.

20
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,000
Can you free me from this pit?

21
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,510
I could.

22
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:15,570
But will I?

23
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:17,450
No.

24
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,140
As I said, I'm no hero.

25
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:21,990
What do you want? Tell me.

26
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:24,840
No riddles, no stories... tell me, what do you want?

27
00:03:26,850 --> 00:03:28,060
Peace.

28
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,540
Did you know that your son is marching south with an army of northmen?

29
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:34,970
Loyal lad...

30
00:03:34,970 --> 00:03:37,200
fighting for his father's freedom.

31
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:38,470
Robb?

32
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,240
He's just a boy.

33
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,820
Boys have been conquerors before.

34
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:46,290
But the man giving Cersei sleepless nights

35
00:03:46,290 --> 00:03:50,490
is the king's... the late king's brother.

36
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:53,500
Lord Stannis has the best claim to the throne,

37
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:56,760
he is a proven battle commander and he is utterly without mercy.

38
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,980
Stannis Baratheon is Robert's true heir.

39
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,960
The throne is his by rights.

40
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:05,920
Sansa pleaded so sweetly for your life,

41
00:04:05,930 --> 00:04:08,100
It would be a shame to throw it away.

42
00:04:09,550 --> 00:04:11,500
Cersei is no fool.

43
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:15,250
She knows a tame wolf is more use to her than a dead one.

44
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,450
You want me to serve the woman who murdered my king,

45
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:20,150
who butchered my men, who crippled my son?

46
00:04:20,150 --> 00:04:22,920
I want you to serve the realm!

47
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,760
Tell the queen you will confess your vile treason,

48
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,720
tell your son to lay down his sword

49
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:30,620
and proclaim Joffrey as the true heir.

50
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:36,130
Cersei knows you as a man of honor.

51
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:38,380
If you give her the peace she needs

52
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:41,020
and promise to carry her secret to your grave,

53
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:43,590
I believe she will allow you to take the black

54
00:04:43,590 --> 00:04:45,510
and live out your days on the wall

55
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:47,540
with your brother and your bastard son.

56
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:51,820
You think my life is some precious thing to me?

57
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:55,970
That I would trade my honor for a few more years of...

58
00:04:56,030 --> 00:04:57,390
Of what?

59
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:04,540
You grew up with actors.

60
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,840
You learned their craft and you learned it well.

61
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:12,540
But I grew up with soldiers.

62
00:05:14,930 --> 00:05:17,570
I learned how to die a long time ago.

63
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,890
Pity.

64
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:25,040
Such a pity.

65
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:34,690
What of your daughter's life, my lord?

66
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:37,120
Is that a precious thing to you?

67
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,230
It's a birthday message to his grand-niece Walda.

68
00:06:21,230 --> 00:06:23,200
Or so Walder Frey would have you think.

69
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,480
Keep shooting them down.

70
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:27,050
We can't risk Lord Walder sending word

71
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:28,060
of your movements to the Lannisters.

72
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:31,200
He's grandfather's bannerman. We can't expect his support?

73
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:35,050
Expect nothing of Walder Frey and you'll never be surprised.

74
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:36,560
Look.

75
00:06:38,550 --> 00:06:40,490
Father rots in a dungeon.

76
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,050
How long before they take his head?

77
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:45,600
We need to cross the Trident and we need to do it now.

78
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:48,200
Just march up to his gates and tell him you're crossing.

79
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,930
We've got five times his numbers.

80
00:06:49,930 --> 00:06:51,450
You can take the Twins if you have to.

81
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:55,040
Not in time. Tywin Lannister marches north as we speak.

82
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,270
The Freys have held the crossing for 600 years,

83
00:06:57,270 --> 00:07:00,800
And for 600 years they have never failed to exact their toll.

84
00:07:01,030 --> 00:07:03,080
Have my horse saddled and ready.

85
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,690
Enter the Twins alone and he'll sell you to the Lannisters,

86
00:07:05,690 --> 00:07:06,860
as he likes.

87
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,770
Or throw you in a dungeon. Or slit your throat.

88
00:07:12,070 --> 00:07:15,140
My father would do whatever it took to secure our crossing.

89
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,700
Whatever it took.

90
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:18,800
If I'm going to lead this army,

91
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:21,440
I can't have other men doing my bargaining for me.

92
00:07:22,190 --> 00:07:23,780
I agree.

93
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,040
I'll go.

94
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:26,800
- Mother. - You can't!

95
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:29,270
I have known Lord Walder since I was a girl.

96
00:07:29,270 --> 00:07:30,890
He would never harm me.

97
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,720
Unless there was a profit in it.

98
00:07:39,450 --> 00:07:40,970
What do you want?

99
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:42,300
It is a great pleasure to

100
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:44,740
see you again after so many years, my lord.

101
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,650
Oh spare me.

102
00:07:47,150 --> 00:07:50,790
Your boy's too proud to come before me himself.

103
00:07:50,810 --> 00:07:52,800
What am I supposed to do with you?

104
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:56,240
Father, you forget yourself. Lady Stark is here...

105
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:59,800
Who asked you? You're not Lord Frey yet,

106
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:02,470
Not until I die. Do I look dead to you?

107
00:08:02,470 --> 00:08:03,410
Father, please...

108
00:08:03,410 --> 00:08:06,930
I need lessons in courtesy from you, bastard?

109
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,670
Your mother would still be a milkmaid

110
00:08:08,670 --> 00:08:11,640
If I hadn't squirted you into her belly.

111
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:18,660
All right, you come forward.

112
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:32,620
There. Now that I've observed the courtesies,

113
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:36,340
Perhaps my sons will do me the honor of shutting their mouths.

114
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,930
Is there somewhere we can talk?

115
00:08:43,930 --> 00:08:45,730
We're talking right now.

116
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,690
Fine.

117
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:54,110
Out! All of you!

118
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:05,520
You too.

119
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,500
You see that?

120
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:16,790
15 she is.

121
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:18,980
A little flower.

122
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:23,180
And her honey's all mine.

123
00:09:25,790 --> 00:09:28,860
I'm sure she will give you many sons.

124
00:09:28,870 --> 00:09:32,070
Huh. Your father didn't come to the wedding.

125
00:09:32,070 --> 00:09:34,040
He is quite ill, my lord.

126
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:37,480
Didn't come to the last one either.

127
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,410
Or the one before that.

128
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,380
Your family has always pissed on me.

129
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:45,050
- My lord, I... - Don't deny it.

130
00:09:45,050 --> 00:09:46,620
You know it's true.

131
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:48,310
The fine Lord Tully

132
00:09:48,310 --> 00:09:51,050
would never marry any of his children to mine.

133
00:09:51,050 --> 00:09:52,510
I'm sure there were reasons why...

134
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:54,440
I didn't need reasons.

135
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,590
I needed to get rid of sons and daughters.

136
00:09:56,590 --> 00:09:58,750
You see how they pile up?

137
00:10:02,730 --> 00:10:04,500
Why are you here?

138
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:07,890
To ask you

139
00:10:07,890 --> 00:10:10,990
to open your gates, my lord,

140
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:14,980
So my son and his bannermen may cross the Trident and be on their way.

141
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:16,250
Why should I let him?

142
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,070
If you could climb your own battlements,

143
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:21,790
you would see that he has 20,000 men outside your walls.

144
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,470
They'll be 20,000 corpses

145
00:10:23,470 --> 00:10:25,280
when Tywin Lannister gets here.

146
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,630
Don't try and frighten me, Lady Stark.

147
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:30,190
Your husband's in a cell beneath the Red Keep

148
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:33,250
and your son's got no fur to keep his balls warm.

149
00:10:33,250 --> 00:10:35,710
You swore an oath to my father.

150
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:38,570
Oh yes, I said some words...

151
00:10:38,730 --> 00:10:42,780
and I swore oaths to the crown too, if I remember right.

152
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:45,870
Joffrey's king now, which makes your boy

153
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:49,690
and his corpses-to-be nothing but rebels, it seems to me.

154
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,080
If I had the sense the gods gave a fish,

155
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,220
I'd hand you both over to the Lannisters.

156
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,460
Why don't you?

157
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,000
Stark, Tully,

158
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,280
Lannister, Baratheon,

159
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:02,770
Give me one good reason

160
00:11:02,770 --> 00:11:05,980
why I should waste a single thought on any of you?

161
00:11:10,850 --> 00:11:13,710
When does Aemon think you'll be able to use that hand?

162
00:11:14,110 --> 00:11:16,740
- Soon, he says. - Good.

163
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,740
You'll be ready for this then.

164
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:25,500
I thought a wolf was more appropriate for you than a bear...

165
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:30,260
So I had a new pommel made. It's called Longclaw.

166
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:34,060
Works as well for a wolf as a bear, I think.

167
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,400
This is Valyrian steel.

168
00:11:47,690 --> 00:11:49,790
It was my father's sword,

169
00:11:49,990 --> 00:11:52,000
his father before him.

170
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
The Mormonts have carried it for five centuries.

171
00:11:55,220 --> 00:11:57,790
It was meant for my son Jorah.

172
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,240
He brought dishonor to our house,

173
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:03,360
but he had the grace to leave the sword

174
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:05,920
before he fled from Westeros.

175
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:08,030
My lord, you honor me, but I can't...

176
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:11,620
Oh, you can and you will.

177
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:13,350
I wouldn't be standing here

178
00:12:13,350 --> 00:12:15,760
if it wasn't for you and your beast.

179
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,920
A bloody dead man tried to kill me...

180
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:24,650
So you'll take it. I'll hear no more about it.

181
00:12:24,810 --> 00:12:27,250
- Is that understood? - Yes, my lord.

182
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:29,780
Right. Now don't think this means

183
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:34,410
I approve of this nonsense with you and Alliser Thorne.

184
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,680
That's a man's sword,

185
00:12:36,930 --> 00:12:38,850
it'll take a man to wield it.

186
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,890
I'll apologize to Ser Alliser tonight.

187
00:12:41,890 --> 00:12:43,410
No, you won't!

188
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,710
I sent him to King's Landing yesterday.

189
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:49,210
The hand that your wolf tore off that thing's wrist...

190
00:12:49,210 --> 00:12:53,090
I've ordered Thorne to lay it at the feet of this...

191
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:54,570
boy king.

192
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,790
That should get young Joffrey's attention.

193
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:03,520
And it puts a thousand leagues between you and Thorne.

194
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:06,600
Now go and put your sword somewhere safe

195
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:09,490
and bring me my supper.

196
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:11,420
Yes, my lord.

197
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:24,710
- Well done. - Well done.

198
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,250
You earned that, Snow.

199
00:13:32,370 --> 00:13:33,910
Well done.

200
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,440
Go on, let's have a look.

201
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:43,070
- At what? - The sword! Show us the sword.

202
00:13:43,070 --> 00:13:49,810
Sword! Sword! Sword! Sword!

203
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:56,110
- Let's have a look. - Piss off.

204
00:13:56,450 --> 00:13:58,120
Get off of it. Piss off.

205
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:01,190
Come on, I want to have a look at it in the light.

206
00:14:05,190 --> 00:14:06,450
Give it here!

207
00:14:07,150 --> 00:14:08,460
What is it?

208
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,750
- I... - Look at its eyes.

209
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,990
- Give it. - I can't.

210
00:14:13,610 --> 00:14:15,190
You can't what?

211
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:20,350
I... I'm really not supposed to say.

212
00:14:20,950 --> 00:14:23,450
And yet you really want to say.

213
00:14:23,930 --> 00:14:26,330
You want to say that...?

214
00:14:29,590 --> 00:14:31,360
There was a raven.

215
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:34,130
I read the message to Maester Aemon.

216
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,660
It's your brother Robb.

217
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,420
What?

218
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:41,680
What about him?

219
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:44,740
He's heading south.

220
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:46,170
To war.

221
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,550
All his bannermen have rallied to his side.

222
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,300
They'll keep him safe.

223
00:14:53,790 --> 00:14:55,550
I should be there.

224
00:14:57,950 --> 00:14:59,610
I should be with him.

225
00:15:14,370 --> 00:15:17,130
If we do that, they'll never get back across.

226
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:19,790
Well?

227
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:22,060
What did he say?

228
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:26,110
Lord Walder has granted your crossing.

229
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:30,750
His men are yours as well...

230
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,120
less the 400 he will keep here to hold the Crossing

231
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,850
against any who would pursue you.

232
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,200
And what does he want in return?

233
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:40,490
You will be taking on his son Olyvar as your personal squire.

234
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:44,020
- He expects a knighthood in good time. - Fine, fine.

235
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:46,970
And?

236
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,490
And Arya

237
00:15:50,490 --> 00:15:52,990
will marry his son Waldron

238
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:54,710
When they both come of age.

239
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,090
She won't be happy about that.

240
00:16:00,550 --> 00:16:01,890
And?

241
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:04,700
And

242
00:16:05,780 --> 00:16:07,800
when the fighting is done...

243
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:12,800
you will marry one of his daughters.

244
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:15,380
Whichever you prefer.

245
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:18,980
He has a number he thinks will be... suitable.

246
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:20,270
I see.

247
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,610
Did you get a look at his daughters?

248
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:26,680
I did.

249
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,100
And?

250
00:16:30,310 --> 00:16:32,300
One was...

251
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,560
Do you consent?

252
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,790
Can I refuse?

253
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,870
Not if you want to cross.

254
00:16:47,150 --> 00:16:49,200
Then I consent.

255
00:17:34,250 --> 00:17:36,150
Sam said you wanted to see me?

256
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:38,290
I did indeed.

257
00:17:38,990 --> 00:17:41,870
Perhaps you would be kind enough to assist me.

258
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:48,140
Tell me, did you ever wonder

259
00:17:48,370 --> 00:17:50,750
why the men of the Night's Watch

260
00:17:50,900 --> 00:17:53,490
take no wives and father no children?

261
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:55,180
No.

262
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:57,880
So they will not love.

263
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:01,290
Love is the death of duty.

264
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,270
If the day should ever come

265
00:18:03,270 --> 00:18:06,090
when your lord father was forced to choose

266
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:08,560
between honor on the one hand

267
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:11,200
and those he loves on the other,

268
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,830
what would he do?

269
00:18:14,590 --> 00:18:18,060
He would do whatever was right. No matter what.

270
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:22,640
Then Lord Stark is one man in 10,000.

271
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:24,840
Most of us are not so strong.

272
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:27,090
What is honor

273
00:18:27,150 --> 00:18:30,350
compared to a woman's love?

274
00:18:30,770 --> 00:18:32,540
And what is duty

275
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:36,510
against the feel of a newborn son in your arms?

276
00:18:36,910 --> 00:18:39,190
Or a brother's smile?

277
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,640
Sam told you.

278
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:46,360
We're all human.

279
00:18:47,050 --> 00:18:49,970
Oh, we all do our duty when there's no cost to it.

280
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:52,490
Honor comes easy then.

281
00:18:52,610 --> 00:18:55,740
Yet sooner or later

282
00:18:56,540 --> 00:18:58,770
in every man's life

283
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:01,990
there comes a day when it is not easy,

284
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:05,310
a day when he must choose.

285
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,750
And this is my day?

286
00:19:09,010 --> 00:19:10,730
Is that what you're saying?

287
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:15,450
Oh, it hurts, boy. Oh yes. I know.

288
00:19:15,450 --> 00:19:17,580
You do not know!

289
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:20,440
No one knows.

290
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:24,950
I may be a bastard,

291
00:19:24,950 --> 00:19:27,960
but he is my father and Robb is my brother.

292
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:35,930
The gods were cruel when they saw fit to test my vows.

293
00:19:36,170 --> 00:19:38,640
They waited till I was old.

294
00:19:39,550 --> 00:19:41,800
What could I do when the ravens brought the news

295
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,830
from the south...

296
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:47,010
The ruin of my house, the death of my family?

297
00:19:47,010 --> 00:19:48,670
I was helpless,

298
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:51,520
blind, frail.

299
00:19:53,450 --> 00:19:56,260
But when I heard

300
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:58,980
they had killed my brother's son,

301
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:01,320
and his poor son...

302
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,150
and the children!

303
00:20:03,150 --> 00:20:05,740
Even the little children.

304
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,230
Who are you?

305
00:20:11,010 --> 00:20:14,850
My father was Maekar,

306
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:17,410
the first of his name.

307
00:20:17,450 --> 00:20:21,530
My brother Aegon reigned after him

308
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:24,450
when I had refused the throne.

309
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:28,000
And he was followed by his son Aerys,

310
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,130
whom they called the Mad King.

311
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:33,570
You're Aemon Targaryen.

312
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:37,480
I'm a maester of the Citadel,

313
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:41,990
bound in service to Castle Black and the Night's Watch.

314
00:20:44,590 --> 00:20:49,390
I will not tell you to stay or go.

315
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:52,410
You must make that choice yourself,

316
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:56,280
and live with it for the rest of your days.

317
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,040
As I have.

318
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:28,640
Drogo.

319
00:21:37,230 --> 00:21:38,830
Sajo anni.

320
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:56,840
Our scouts tell us

321
00:22:56,840 --> 00:22:59,500
the Stark host has moved south from the Twins

322
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,920
with Lord Frey's levies in tow.

323
00:23:01,930 --> 00:23:03,850
They're a day's march north.

324
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:07,110
The boy may lack experience and sense,

325
00:23:07,110 --> 00:23:09,950
but he does have a certain mindless

326
00:23:10,690 --> 00:23:14,040
provincial courage.

327
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:19,200
Oh, do continue. Didn't mean to interrupt.

328
00:23:19,210 --> 00:23:21,670
I do hope your savages are going to be of some use,

329
00:23:21,670 --> 00:23:23,780
otherwise we've wasted good steel on them.

330
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:27,380
The great hairy one insisted he must have two battleaxes...

331
00:23:27,380 --> 00:23:28,860
heavy black steel,

332
00:23:28,870 --> 00:23:29,820
double-sided.

333
00:23:29,820 --> 00:23:31,680
Shagga likes axes.

334
00:23:32,050 --> 00:23:33,540
When the battle commences,

335
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:36,520
you and your wildlings will be in the vanguard.

336
00:23:36,530 --> 00:23:38,310
The vanguard?

337
00:23:38,310 --> 00:23:40,930
Me and the tribesmen on the front lines?

338
00:23:40,930 --> 00:23:43,630
They do seem rather ferocious.

339
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:49,360
Ferocious? Last night

340
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:51,620
a Moon Brother stabbed a Stone Crow

341
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:52,920
over a sausage.

342
00:23:52,980 --> 00:23:54,710
Three Stone Crows seized the Moon Brother

343
00:23:54,710 --> 00:23:56,170
and opened his throat.

344
00:23:56,170 --> 00:23:57,280
Bronn managed to keep

345
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:59,270
Shagga from chopping off the dead man's cock,

346
00:23:59,270 --> 00:24:01,560
which was fortunate, but even still

347
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:03,590
Ulf is demanding blood money,

348
00:24:03,590 --> 00:24:06,070
which Shagga and Gunthor refuse to pay.

349
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:07,470
When soldiers lack discipline,

350
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,420
the fault lies with their commander.

351
00:24:09,420 --> 00:24:10,930
Surely there are ways to have me killed

352
00:24:10,930 --> 00:24:12,800
that would be less detrimental to the war effort.

353
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:15,040
There'll be no more discussion on the matter.

354
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,710
It appears I'm not hungry after all.

355
00:24:22,780 --> 00:24:24,300
Excuse me, my lords.

356
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:40,930
Where did you find one so pretty at this hour?

357
00:24:40,930 --> 00:24:43,580
- I took her. - Took her?

358
00:24:43,810 --> 00:24:46,440
- From whom? - From, uh...

359
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:50,130
Ser... what's his name? I don't know.

360
00:24:50,130 --> 00:24:52,230
Ginger cunt three tents down.

361
00:24:52,230 --> 00:24:54,970
And he didn't have anything to say about it?

362
00:24:55,590 --> 00:24:57,220
He said something.

363
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:03,080
Well, the odds of me living long enough

364
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:05,750
for him to retaliate just dropped drastically.

365
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:07,970
We'll be at the vanguard tomorrow.

366
00:25:10,930 --> 00:25:12,240
Oh well.

367
00:25:14,370 --> 00:25:18,430
I... think I'll go and find myself one.

368
00:25:22,330 --> 00:25:23,790
Who are you?

369
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:25,850
Who would you like me to be?

370
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,070
What did your mother call you?

371
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:31,890
Shae. what did your mother call you?

372
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:34,180
My mother died giving birth to me.

373
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:37,880
Is that why I'm here? So we can talk about our mothers?

374
00:25:38,490 --> 00:25:41,510
- What sort of accent is that? - Foreign.

375
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:43,310
For...

376
00:25:44,670 --> 00:25:46,400
What do you want from me?

377
00:25:46,940 --> 00:25:49,030
What do I want from you?

378
00:25:50,530 --> 00:25:52,600
I want you to share my tent.

379
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:55,500
I want you to pour my wine, laugh at my jokes,

380
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:58,400
rub my legs when they're sore after a day's ride.

381
00:25:58,710 --> 00:26:00,800
I want you to take no other man to bed

382
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,310
for as long as we're together.

383
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:03,980
And I want you to fuck me

384
00:26:03,980 --> 00:26:06,910
like it's my last night in this world...

385
00:26:06,910 --> 00:26:08,800
which it may well be.

386
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:10,890
And what do I get?

387
00:26:11,010 --> 00:26:12,730
One, safety.

388
00:26:13,670 --> 00:26:16,690
No one will hurt you for as long as you're mine.

389
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:20,440
Two. The pleasure of my company,

390
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:22,930
which I have heard is spectacular.

391
00:26:22,930 --> 00:26:25,420
Who told you this? Women you paid?

392
00:26:25,420 --> 00:26:26,750
And three.

393
00:26:27,060 --> 00:26:31,420
More gold than you can spend if you lived a thousand years.

394
00:26:32,790 --> 00:26:35,170
Do you accept my proposal?

395
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:57,570
Let's start with your last night in this world.

396
00:27:16,550 --> 00:27:21,250
Doth... dothra... ki

397
00:27:21,250 --> 00:27:22,570
Ha... hammi...

398
00:27:24,140 --> 00:27:26,060
Ish nokitta...

399
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:28,280
Qana'th...

400
00:27:29,490 --> 00:27:31,010
Khaleesi.

401
00:27:31,530 --> 00:27:32,740
Come.

402
00:27:34,910 --> 00:27:36,800
He's very strong.

403
00:27:36,870 --> 00:27:40,190
No one understands how strong he is.

404
00:27:59,180 --> 00:28:02,270
- He will die tonight, Khaleesi. - He can't.

405
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:04,990
He can't. I won't let him.

406
00:28:05,050 --> 00:28:07,720
Even a queen doesn't have that power.

407
00:28:10,670 --> 00:28:14,310
We must go quickly. I've heard there's a good port in Asshai...

408
00:28:14,310 --> 00:28:18,090
- I won't leave him. - He's already gone, Khaleesi.

409
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:19,850
Doth...

410
00:28:20,550 --> 00:28:22,340
Even if...

411
00:28:23,980 --> 00:28:26,080
even if he dies,

412
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:28,800
why would I run?

413
00:28:29,230 --> 00:28:30,730
I am Khaleesi

414
00:28:30,730 --> 00:28:34,210
and my... my son will be Khal after Drogo.

415
00:28:34,210 --> 00:28:37,380
This isn't Westeros where men honor blood.

416
00:28:37,380 --> 00:28:39,160
Here they only honor strength.

417
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:41,870
There will be fighting after Drogo dies.

418
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:44,800
Whoever wins that fight will be the new Khal.

419
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:46,910
He won't want any rivals.

420
00:28:46,910 --> 00:28:49,440
Your boy will be plucked from your breast

421
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:51,420
and given to the dogs.

422
00:28:52,540 --> 00:28:55,390
I won't leave him.

423
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:07,320
The wound has festered.

424
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:10,570
I think you should wear your armor tonight, Ser.

425
00:30:11,350 --> 00:30:12,960
I think you're right.

426
00:30:18,540 --> 00:30:20,300
You've saved me once more.

427
00:30:20,300 --> 00:30:22,600
And now you must save him.

428
00:30:22,850 --> 00:30:24,880
He's beyond the healer's skills.

429
00:30:25,180 --> 00:30:27,480
All I can do is ease his path.

430
00:30:27,490 --> 00:30:30,060
Save him and I will free you. I swear it.

431
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:32,610
You must know a way...

432
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:37,410
some...  some magic.

433
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:41,120
There is a spell.

434
00:30:42,050 --> 00:30:44,220
Some would say death is cleaner.

435
00:30:54,730 --> 00:30:56,040
Do it.

436
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:58,080
Save him.

437
00:30:58,830 --> 00:30:59,670
There is a price.

438
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:01,460
You'll have gold... whatever you want.

439
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:04,040
It's not a matter of gold. This is bloodmagic.

440
00:31:04,040 --> 00:31:06,270
Only death pays for life.

441
00:31:09,550 --> 00:31:11,210
My death?

442
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:14,240
No. Not your death, Khaleesi.

443
00:31:15,650 --> 00:31:17,550
Bring me his horse.

444
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:43,200
Khaleesi, do not do this thing.

445
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:44,500
Let me kill this witch.

446
00:31:44,500 --> 00:31:46,440
Kill her and you kill your Khal.

447
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:49,110
This is bloodmagic. It is forbidden.

448
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:53,200
I am your Khaleesi. I tell you what is forbidden.

449
00:32:03,300 --> 00:32:05,120
Go now!

450
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:06,710
Take her and leave.

451
00:32:06,710 --> 00:32:08,220
Take her!

452
00:32:11,080 --> 00:32:12,420
Irri a?

453
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:15,250
You must go also, lady.

454
00:32:15,260 --> 00:32:17,920
Once I begin to sing, no one must enter the tent.

455
00:32:17,950 --> 00:32:20,870
The dead will dance here tonight.

456
00:32:33,630 --> 00:32:35,430
No one will enter.

457
00:32:44,220 --> 00:32:46,120
bring him back to me.

458
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:04,550
What have you done?

459
00:33:04,560 --> 00:33:06,340
I have to save him.

460
00:33:06,700 --> 00:33:08,160
We could have been 10 miles

461
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:10,290
away from here by now on the way to Asshai.

462
00:33:10,300 --> 00:33:11,940
You would have been safe.

463
00:33:18,510 --> 00:33:20,140
Jni'th vos eo.

464
00:33:24,780 --> 00:33:26,690
Mra qothoon vosaan

465
00:33:29,700 --> 00:33:30,900
Khaleesi!

466
00:34:15,340 --> 00:34:16,680
Are you hurt?

467
00:34:16,680 --> 00:34:17,900
The baby...

468
00:34:17,900 --> 00:34:19,260
...is coming.

469
00:34:19,460 --> 00:34:21,840
- Fetch the midwives. - they will not come.

470
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:23,520
They say she is cursed.

471
00:34:24,890 --> 00:34:27,100
They'll come or I'll have their heads.

472
00:34:28,150 --> 00:34:30,360
The witch... she can bring baby.

473
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:32,130
I hear her say so.

474
00:34:55,450 --> 00:34:57,980
- Are you in agony, my lion? - No.

475
00:34:57,980 --> 00:34:59,930
You look like you're in agony.

476
00:35:00,420 --> 00:35:02,990
The fire is burning your pretty soft skin.

477
00:35:09,860 --> 00:35:12,690
Damn you, woman. Are you immune to pain?

478
00:35:12,690 --> 00:35:14,870
- Just used to it. - Drink.

479
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,200
Let's play a new game.

480
00:35:20,240 --> 00:35:23,220
There's a Braavosi knife game I could teach you...

481
00:35:23,220 --> 00:35:25,920
Does it involve the potential for losing fingers?

482
00:35:26,110 --> 00:35:28,620
- Not if you win. - No!

483
00:35:28,690 --> 00:35:31,490
No more fire games, no knife games.

484
00:35:32,330 --> 00:35:34,420
Let's do something I'm good at.

485
00:35:34,460 --> 00:35:36,310
What are you good at?

486
00:35:36,560 --> 00:35:38,770
I happen to be a great judge of character.

487
00:35:38,770 --> 00:35:41,030
- This sounds like a boring game. - It's not.

488
00:35:41,030 --> 00:35:44,830
Here's how it works: I make a statement about your past.

489
00:35:44,830 --> 00:35:48,190
If I'm right, you drink. If I'm wrong, I drink.

490
00:35:48,190 --> 00:35:51,430
And no lying. I'll know if you're lying.

491
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:53,080
I don't want to play this game.

492
00:35:53,080 --> 00:35:55,270
Fine. Bronn first.

493
00:35:59,710 --> 00:36:01,790
Your father beat you.

494
00:36:07,230 --> 00:36:09,380
But my mother hit harder.

495
00:36:12,650 --> 00:36:15,320
You killed your first man before you were 12.

496
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:16,950
It was a woman.

497
00:36:20,470 --> 00:36:22,410
She swung an axe at me.

498
00:36:23,390 --> 00:36:25,390
You've been north of the Wall.

499
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:30,480
What brought you up there?

500
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:32,730
Work.

501
00:36:32,730 --> 00:36:33,910
And...

502
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:36,580
you once loved a woman many years ago,

503
00:36:36,580 --> 00:36:40,220
but it turned out badly so you've never let yourself love again.

504
00:36:42,290 --> 00:36:44,440
Oh wait, that's me.

505
00:36:47,670 --> 00:36:50,360
Your turn, my mysterious foreign beauty.

506
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:52,070
I don't want to play.

507
00:36:52,070 --> 00:36:56,260
It's fun! Look at the fun we're having.

508
00:36:59,290 --> 00:37:01,080
Your mother was a whore.

509
00:37:02,350 --> 00:37:03,760
Drink.

510
00:37:10,050 --> 00:37:11,420
All right.

511
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:14,900
Your father left the family when you were very young,

512
00:37:14,900 --> 00:37:17,760
- never to return. - Drink.

513
00:37:18,190 --> 00:37:21,760
- And we've established the rules about lying? - Drink!

514
00:37:28,710 --> 00:37:30,110
You wanted a different life.

515
00:37:30,110 --> 00:37:33,120
You came from somewhere and you wanted to be elsewhere.

516
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:35,480
The whole shit-stained world could drink off that one.

517
00:37:35,490 --> 00:37:37,320
So specifics...

518
00:37:37,980 --> 00:37:41,070
you wanted to be elsewhere, but how would you get there?

519
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:45,250
I don't believe the life of the silent sisters is for you.

520
00:37:45,510 --> 00:37:49,790
So what's a lowborn girl to do?

521
00:37:52,860 --> 00:37:54,390
Drink.

522
00:37:56,840 --> 00:37:58,960
- Are you sure... - Drink!

523
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:07,950
And don't talk about my mother and father ever

524
00:38:08,100 --> 00:38:11,150
or I will carve your eyes from your head.

525
00:38:15,010 --> 00:38:18,300
My dear lady, if I have offended you, I apologize.

526
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,620
My turn.

527
00:38:20,620 --> 00:38:22,590
Fine fine.

528
00:38:22,660 --> 00:38:24,240
Ask away.

529
00:38:24,930 --> 00:38:27,810
Try to penetrate the enigma that is me.

530
00:38:27,810 --> 00:38:31,080
- Who were you in love with? - That's not how the game works.

531
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:33,290
I don't care the way the game works.

532
00:38:33,290 --> 00:38:35,960
Our lord here used to be married.

533
00:38:36,420 --> 00:38:38,790
- Married? - How did you hear that?

534
00:38:38,790 --> 00:38:42,450
You hear lots of things playing dice with Lannister soldiers.

535
00:38:44,550 --> 00:38:46,440
Another night, perhaps.

536
00:38:47,110 --> 00:38:49,710
Not another night. This night.

537
00:38:50,950 --> 00:38:52,860
It's not a pleasant story.

538
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:55,810
Or maybe I will cry.

539
00:38:55,810 --> 00:38:57,480
I'm guessing the lady and I

540
00:38:57,480 --> 00:39:00,490
can tell more unpleasant stories than your lordship.

541
00:39:02,690 --> 00:39:04,100
So...

542
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:11,630
I was 16. My brother Jaime and I were riding

543
00:39:11,630 --> 00:39:16,010
when we heard a scream. She ran out onto the road,

544
00:39:16,010 --> 00:39:19,130
clothes half torn off with two men on her heels.

545
00:39:19,130 --> 00:39:20,910
Jaime scared away the men easily enough,

546
00:39:20,910 --> 00:39:23,060
while I wrapped her in my cloak.

547
00:39:23,250 --> 00:39:25,000
She was too scared to send off on her own,

548
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:27,700
so while Jaime hunted down the rapers

549
00:39:27,700 --> 00:39:30,160
I took her to the nearest inn and fed her.

550
00:39:30,630 --> 00:39:32,330
Her name was Tysha.

551
00:39:32,720 --> 00:39:34,890
She was a wheelwright's orphan.

552
00:39:35,150 --> 00:39:37,200
And she was hungry...

553
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:40,840
together we finished off three chickens and a flagon of wine.

554
00:39:40,850 --> 00:39:42,080
Impossible as it seems,

555
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:44,720
there was a time when I was unaccustomed to wine.

556
00:39:45,260 --> 00:39:48,140
I forgot how afraid I was around girls,

557
00:39:48,260 --> 00:39:50,560
how I was always waiting for them to laugh at me

558
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:52,930
or look away embarrassed

559
00:39:52,940 --> 00:39:55,790
or ask me about my tall handsome brother.

560
00:39:56,200 --> 00:39:58,810
I forgot about everything but Tysha.

561
00:39:59,490 --> 00:40:02,410
And somehow I found myself in her bed.

562
00:40:02,410 --> 00:40:04,880
For three chickens, I should hope so.

563
00:40:05,490 --> 00:40:08,510
It didn't last long. I didn't know what the hell I was doing.

564
00:40:08,930 --> 00:40:10,810
But she was good to me.

565
00:40:11,010 --> 00:40:12,380
She kissed me afterwards

566
00:40:12,380 --> 00:40:15,670
and sang me a song.

567
00:40:17,140 --> 00:40:21,350
And by morning I was deep enough in love to ask for her hand.

568
00:40:21,490 --> 00:40:23,260
A few lies, a few gold coins,

569
00:40:23,260 --> 00:40:24,100
one drunken septon

570
00:40:24,100 --> 00:40:26,480
and there you have it... man and wife.

571
00:40:27,720 --> 00:40:29,940
For a fortnight anyway, until the septon sobered up

572
00:40:29,950 --> 00:40:32,000
and told my father.

573
00:40:33,230 --> 00:40:35,390
I imagine that was the end of all that.

574
00:40:35,390 --> 00:40:36,910
Not quite.

575
00:40:38,090 --> 00:40:41,210
First, my father had Jaime tell me the truth.

576
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:44,930
The girl was a whore, you see.

577
00:40:46,510 --> 00:40:49,030
Jaime had arranged the whole thing,

578
00:40:49,030 --> 00:40:52,080
the road, the rapers... all of it.

579
00:40:52,100 --> 00:40:54,770
He thought it was time I had a woman.

580
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:58,660
After my brother confessed,

581
00:40:59,610 --> 00:41:01,470
my father brought in my wife

582
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:04,190
and gave her to his guards.

583
00:41:04,970 --> 00:41:08,000
He paid her well... a silver for each man.

584
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:11,120
How many whores command that kind of price?

585
00:41:12,790 --> 00:41:16,140
He brought me into the barracks and made me watch.

586
00:41:16,570 --> 00:41:19,820
By the end, she had so much silver

587
00:41:19,820 --> 00:41:22,280
that the coins were slipping through her fingers

588
00:41:22,280 --> 00:41:24,930
and rolling onto the floor.

589
00:41:28,440 --> 00:41:31,540
I would have killed the man who did that to me.

590
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:34,610
You should have known she was a whore.

591
00:41:35,250 --> 00:41:36,730
Really?

592
00:41:37,080 --> 00:41:40,000
I was 16, drunk and in love...

593
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:41,420
A girl who was almost raped

594
00:41:41,420 --> 00:41:45,000
doesn't invite another man into her bed two hours later.

595
00:41:46,190 --> 00:41:50,430
As I said, I was young and stupid.

596
00:41:52,560 --> 00:41:55,220
You are still young and stupid.

597
00:42:37,130 --> 00:42:38,650
What is it? What do you want?

598
00:42:38,650 --> 00:42:40,440
You're sleeping through the war.

599
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:42,920
- What? - They stole a night's march on us.

600
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:44,600
They're a mile north.

601
00:42:45,580 --> 00:42:48,150
- Get my squire! - You don't have a squire.

602
00:42:50,620 --> 00:42:52,990
If I die, weep for me.

603
00:42:53,980 --> 00:42:57,530
You'll be dead. How will you know?

604
00:43:03,250 --> 00:43:04,760
I'll know.

605
00:43:07,450 --> 00:43:09,270
Watch out! Move!

606
00:43:10,050 --> 00:43:11,360
Out of the way!

607
00:43:11,810 --> 00:43:13,800
Move aside!

608
00:43:20,050 --> 00:43:21,390
Stay low.

609
00:43:22,520 --> 00:43:23,980
Stay low?

610
00:43:24,280 --> 00:43:26,500
If you're lucky, no one will notice you.

611
00:43:26,880 --> 00:43:28,730
I was born lucky.

612
00:43:31,660 --> 00:43:33,490
Tribesmen of the Vale,

613
00:43:34,020 --> 00:43:35,610
Gather round!

614
00:43:37,350 --> 00:43:39,250
Stone Crows!

615
00:43:39,310 --> 00:43:41,960
Black Ears! Burned Men!

616
00:43:42,090 --> 00:43:43,460
Moon Brothers!

617
00:43:44,470 --> 00:43:46,350
And painted dogs!

618
00:43:47,210 --> 00:43:50,770
Your dominion over the Vale begins now!

619
00:43:50,770 --> 00:43:53,410
Onward to claim what is yours!

620
00:43:53,550 --> 00:43:56,040
half man! Half man!

621
00:43:56,040 --> 00:43:59,170
Half man! Half man!

622
00:43:59,170 --> 00:44:01,990
Half man! Half man!

623
00:44:02,090 --> 00:44:03,490
To battle.

624
00:44:46,340 --> 00:44:48,040
You're a shit warrior.

625
00:44:51,300 --> 00:44:52,900
I'm alive?

626
00:44:53,690 --> 00:44:55,170
You're alive.

627
00:45:00,600 --> 00:45:01,980
Did we win?

628
00:45:02,420 --> 00:45:04,940
We wouldn't be having this conversation if we didn't.

629
00:45:18,080 --> 00:45:20,100
How did our tribesmen do?

630
00:45:21,890 --> 00:45:23,680
Yeah, good.

631
00:45:25,160 --> 00:45:27,390
It's nice to see them getting along.

632
00:45:27,870 --> 00:45:29,580
You're wounded.

633
00:45:30,420 --> 00:45:32,410
Good of you to notice.

634
00:45:33,260 --> 00:45:34,820
I hear we won.

635
00:45:34,860 --> 00:45:37,690
Hmph. The scouts were wrong.

636
00:45:37,690 --> 00:45:41,620
There were 2,000 Stark bannermen, not 20,000.

637
00:45:42,230 --> 00:45:44,490
Did we get the Stark boy, at least?

638
00:45:44,490 --> 00:45:46,010
He wasn't here.

639
00:45:46,680 --> 00:45:48,360
Where was he?

640
00:45:48,610 --> 00:45:51,500
With his other 18,000 men.

641
00:45:54,570 --> 00:45:56,180
And where are they?

642
00:46:06,820 --> 00:46:09,010
- We should go, my lady. - No!

643
00:46:13,930 --> 00:46:15,570
My lady!

644
00:46:51,120 --> 00:46:52,450
By the time they knew what was happening,

645
00:46:52,450 --> 00:46:54,180
it had already happened.

646
00:46:58,600 --> 00:47:01,000
Lady Stark. I'd offer you my sword,

647
00:47:01,000 --> 00:47:02,490
but I seem to have lost it.

648
00:47:02,490 --> 00:47:04,940
It's not your sword I want.

649
00:47:06,090 --> 00:47:08,030
Give me my daughters back.

650
00:47:08,030 --> 00:47:09,790
Give me my husband.

651
00:47:10,950 --> 00:47:12,650
I've lost them too, I'm afraid.

652
00:47:12,650 --> 00:47:14,990
Kill him, Robb. Send his head to his father.

653
00:47:14,990 --> 00:47:17,760
He cut down 10 of our men... you saw him.

654
00:47:17,760 --> 00:47:20,120
He's more use to us alive than dead.

655
00:47:20,160 --> 00:47:22,520
Take him away and put him in irons.

656
00:47:23,420 --> 00:47:25,850
We could end this war right now, boy,

657
00:47:25,860 --> 00:47:27,960
save thousands of lives.

658
00:47:27,960 --> 00:47:29,070
You fight for the Starks,

659
00:47:29,070 --> 00:47:30,870
I fight for the Lannisters.

660
00:47:30,880 --> 00:47:34,350
Swords or lances, teeth, nails... choose your weapons

661
00:47:34,350 --> 00:47:36,750
and let's end this here and now.

662
00:47:39,210 --> 00:47:41,590
If we do it your way, Kingslayer,

663
00:47:42,390 --> 00:47:44,100
you'd win.

664
00:47:47,220 --> 00:47:49,390
We're not doing it your way.

665
00:47:50,770 --> 00:47:52,970
Come on, pretty man.

666
00:48:01,530 --> 00:48:04,210
I sent 2,000 men to their graves today.

667
00:48:04,210 --> 00:48:06,690
The bards will sing songs of their sacrifice.

668
00:48:06,690 --> 00:48:10,170
Aye. But the dead won't hear them.

669
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:19,650
One victory does not make us conquerors.

670
00:48:21,130 --> 00:48:23,340
Did we free my father?

671
00:48:24,060 --> 00:48:26,820
Did we rescue my sisters from the queen?

672
00:48:28,070 --> 00:48:32,110
Did we free the north from those who want us on our knees?

673
00:48:37,020 --> 00:48:39,350
This war is far from over.

674
00:49:10,720 --> 00:49:12,230
Could I have one?

675
00:49:12,320 --> 00:49:14,460
A lemon one... or any of them.

676
00:49:14,460 --> 00:49:16,020
Three coppers.

677
00:49:16,700 --> 00:49:18,330
How about a nice fat pigeon?

678
00:49:18,330 --> 00:49:20,130
Piss off now. Go on.

679
00:49:21,500 --> 00:49:23,470
Do you have any stale ones from yesterday?

680
00:49:23,470 --> 00:49:26,090
- Or any burnt ones? - Piss off!

681
00:49:33,580 --> 00:49:35,600
Hey, where's everyone going? What's happening?

682
00:49:35,600 --> 00:49:37,830
- They're taking him to the Sept Of Baelor. - Who?

683
00:49:37,830 --> 00:49:39,520
The hand of the king.

684
00:50:47,620 --> 00:50:49,640
- Traitor! - Coward!

685
00:50:49,840 --> 00:50:50,940
Baelor.

686
00:50:51,740 --> 00:50:53,070
Baelor!

687
00:50:59,290 --> 00:51:02,350
Traitor! Traitor!

688
00:51:21,280 --> 00:51:23,270
I am Eddard Stark,

689
00:51:23,870 --> 00:51:25,700
Lord of Winterfell

690
00:51:25,870 --> 00:51:27,740
and Hand of the King.

691
00:51:37,140 --> 00:51:40,440
I come before you to confess my treason

692
00:51:40,870 --> 00:51:43,100
in the sight of gods and men.

693
00:51:44,780 --> 00:51:47,410
I betrayed the faith of my king

694
00:51:47,600 --> 00:51:49,970
and the trust of my friend Robert.

695
00:51:51,080 --> 00:51:54,130
I swore to proct and defend his children,

696
00:51:54,430 --> 00:51:56,910
but before his blood was cold

697
00:51:57,470 --> 00:51:59,770
I plotted to murder his son...

698
00:52:00,760 --> 00:52:02,900
and seize the throne for myself.

699
00:52:04,520 --> 00:52:05,910
Traitor!

700
00:52:13,900 --> 00:52:15,790
Let the High Septon

701
00:52:15,790 --> 00:52:19,540
and Baelor the Blessed bear witness to what I say:

702
00:52:22,180 --> 00:52:24,050
Joffrey Baratheon

703
00:52:25,290 --> 00:52:28,310
is the one true heir to the Iron Throne,

704
00:52:28,480 --> 00:52:30,850
By the grace of all the gods,

705
00:52:31,210 --> 00:52:33,460
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms

706
00:52:34,000 --> 00:52:36,190
and Protector of the Realm.

707
00:52:43,200 --> 00:52:45,630
As we sin,

708
00:52:45,920 --> 00:52:47,790
so do we suffer.

709
00:52:47,800 --> 00:52:50,820
This man has confessed his crimes

710
00:52:50,820 --> 00:52:53,910
in sight of gods and men.

711
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,650
The gods are just

712
00:52:56,660 --> 00:53:00,190
but Beloved Baelor taught us

713
00:53:00,190 --> 00:53:03,440
they can also be merciful.

714
00:53:06,220 --> 00:53:07,780
What is to be done

715
00:53:07,780 --> 00:53:11,180
with this traitor, your grace?

716
00:53:15,230 --> 00:53:18,700
My mother wishes me to let Lord Eddard join the Night's Watch.

717
00:53:18,800 --> 00:53:20,690
Stripped of all titles and powers,

718
00:53:20,690 --> 00:53:23,210
he would serve the realm in permanent exile.

719
00:53:23,560 --> 00:53:25,500
And my lady Sansa

720
00:53:26,170 --> 00:53:28,670
has begged mercy for her father.

721
00:53:32,700 --> 00:53:35,390
But they have the soft hearts of women.

722
00:53:36,200 --> 00:53:38,330
So long as I am your king,

723
00:53:38,510 --> 00:53:41,750
treason shall never go unpunished.

724
00:53:42,160 --> 00:53:43,830
Ser Ilyn,

725
00:53:44,740 --> 00:53:46,110
bring me his head!

726
00:53:46,110 --> 00:53:47,610
No! Stop!

727
00:53:48,270 --> 00:53:50,600
Please! Someone stop him!

728
00:54:01,680 --> 00:54:03,760
My son, this is madness.

729
00:54:04,340 --> 00:54:06,060
Put him down!

730
00:54:13,340 --> 00:54:14,940
- Don't look! - Let me go.

731
00:54:14,940 --> 00:54:17,680
- Let me go! - Shut your mouth. Look at me.

732
00:54:17,690 --> 00:54:20,230
- Look at me! - Stop! Daddy!

733
00:54:20,230 --> 00:54:22,990
- Stop! No no! - Traitor!

734
00:54:22,990 --> 00:54:24,150
Stop!

735
00:54:27,920 --> 00:54:29,930
Stop him, stop!

